<title>INDIA: Bombay cotton markets closed for Moslem holiday.</title>
<headline>Bombay cotton markets closed for Moslem holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombay's cotton markets were closed on Friday for a Moslem festival.</p>
<p>On Thursday, cotton prices remained steady in limited activity but sentiment was subdued amid poor mill buying and the absence of fresh export quotas by Indian government.</p>
<p>Traders estimate the unsold stock of cotton across the country at 2.40/2.50 million bales (170 kg each).</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
